{"filePath":"/home/john/mynotes/shadow_frontier/notes/cic_roundchain.tex","newString":"\\section{The $3$-smooth cascade and the $2$-adic logarithm calculus}\n\nThe Mersenne theorem extends to the full $3$-smooth neighborhoods\n$x=2^g3^a\\mp1$ --- and the cascade goes \\emph{deeper} than one round.\nAll statements below are machine-verified\n(\\texttt{search/smooth\\_cascade.py}; grids $g<42$, $a<26$, and the\none-parameter family to $n\\le3000$).\n\n\\begin{theorem}[Minus family]\\label{thm:minus}\nFor $x=2^g3^a-1$ ($g\\ge2$) the entire round chain depends on $(g,a)$\nonly through $n=g+a-1$ (the chain sees $m,\\ell$ only through\n$3^\\ell m=3^n$). The first reading is $v=\\vt(3^n-1)$, given by LTE:\n$v=1$ for $n$ odd, $v=2+\\vt(n)$ for $n$ even; survival iff $\\vt(n)$\nis even $\\ge2$, of density $\\tfrac16$ over $n$ --- the family is\nghost-aligned and dies at $2\\times$ the Haar rate in round one. The\nround-$2$ reading is the $4$-term $S$-unit valuation\n\\[\nv'=\\vt\\bigl(3^{\\,n+r+\\ell'}-3^{\\,r+\\ell'}+2^{v}3^{\\ell'}-2^{\\,v+\\ell'}\\bigr)\n-v-\\ell' .\n\\]\n\\end{theorem}\n\n\\begin{theorem}[Plus family]\\label{thm:plus}\nFor $x=2^g3^a+1$ ($g\\ge3$) the $+1$ clock rides\n$\\lfloor(g-1)/2\\rfloor$ blocks ending $3$-smooth, with\n$a'=a+\\lfloor(g-1)/2\\rfloor$:\n\\begin{itemize}\n\\item[(i)] $g$ even: terminal $4\\cdot3^{a'}+1$, death letter\n$b=2+\\vt(3^{a'+1}+1)\\in\\{3,4\\}$ by LTE --- closed-form CIC death.\n\\item[(ii)] $g$ odd: lands at $2\\cdot3^{a'}+1$, next depth $g'=2$\n($a'$ even) or $3$ ($a'$ odd). If $a'$ is even the round-$2$ reading\nis $v'=\\vt(3^{a'+1}+1)-1=1$: closed-form death. If $a'$ is odd,\n\\[\nv'=\\vt\\bigl(3^{a'+2}+5\\bigr)-2\n=\\vt\\bigl(a'+2-\\mathrm{Log}_3(-5)\\bigr):\n\\]\n\\emph{the survival reading is the $2$-adic alignment of the exponent\nto the $2$-adic logarithm of the ghost $-5$}, where\n$N_0=\\mathrm{Log}_3(-5)=2556611305511861515 \\bmod 2^{64}$ and\n$\\vt(3^N+5)=2+\\vt(N-N_0)$ for $N\\equiv N_0\\bmod2$.\n\\end{itemize}\n\\end{theorem}\n\n\\begin{proposition}[The $S$-unit horizon]\\label{prop:horizon}\nAlong any $3$-smooth-seeded chain, the round-$j$ reading is the\n$2$-adic valuation of a $2$--$3$ $S$-unit form whose term count grows\nwith $j$; two-term forms are LTE (closed), and the collapsed cases\nreduce to alignments of integer exponents to $2$-adic logarithms of\nghosts. The deterministic horizon of the cascade is exactly the\n$S$-unit term count the machinery can close --- the CIC on these\nfamilies meets the banded $S$-unit frontier (Target 1) at the level of\n\\emph{exponents}, where effective $p$-adic Baker theory (Yu) bounds\nevery reading by $O(\\log)$ of the exponent height.\n\\end{proposition}\n\n\\noindent\\emph{Cascade statistics} (one-parameter family, $n\\le3000$):\nsurvival $0.16633$ after round $1$ (LTE prediction $\\tfrac16$), then\nconditional survivals $0.34,\\ 0.31,\\ 0.40,\\ 0.19,\\ 0.25$ --- the\nre-randomized fair-thirds coin of \\cref{thm:iid}. The champion is\n$n=704$, surviving $6$ rounds with readings $[8,2,2,2,2,2,3]$;\n\\emph{every} $n\\le3000$ dies by round $7$: the CIC holds, with\nexplicit finite certificates, for the entire $3$-smooth slice tested.\nThe ghost hierarchy thus lifts one level: at the base, integers align\nto ghosts ($-1$, $+1$, $-5$, \\dots); at the exponent level, exponents\nalign to $2$-adic logarithms of ghosts; survival is a parity reading\nat each level, deterministic exactly where freshness fails.\n\n\\section{Where the wall now stands}","oldString":"\\section{Where the wall now stands}","originalFile":"\\documentclass[11pt]{article}\n\\usepackage[margin=2.4cm]{geometry}\n\\usepackage{amsmath,amssymb,amsthm,booktabs}\n\\usepackage[capitalize]{cleveref}\n\\newtheorem{theorem}{Theorem}\n\\newtheorem{lemma}{Lemma}\n\\newtheorem{proposition}{Proposition}\n\\newtheorem{corollary}{Corollary}\n\\newtheorem{conjecture}{Conjecture}\n\\newtheorem*{remark}{Remark}\n\\newcommand{\\vt}{v_2}\n\\title{The Carry Independence Conjecture in Two-Clock Form:\\\\\nthe LTE round chain, exact Haar laws, and the entropy deficit}\n\\author{John A. Janik\\\\ \\small\\texttt{john.janik@gmail.com}}\n\\date{June 2026}\n\\begin{document}\n\\maketitle\n\n\\begin{abstract}\nThe Carry Independence Conjecture (CIC) of arXiv:2603.11066 --- every\nodd $n_0>1$ eventually takes a Syracuse letter $b\\ge3$ --- is the\nweakest nontrivial case of our two-clock calibration conjecture (it\nasserts the handoff parity cannot equal $1$ forever). We attack it\nwith the lifting-the-exponent machinery. Results: (1) convergent\norbits satisfy the CIC automatically (every entry into $1$ uses a\nletter $b\\ge4$), so the CIC concerns only divergent $\\{1,2\\}$-orbits;\n(2) a $\\{1,2\\}$-orbit is exactly an iterated chain of odd integers in\nwhich each survival event is the LTE reading\n$\\vt(3^\\ell m-1)=\\vt(m-3^{-\\ell})$ --- alignment of the orbit's fresh\nhigh bits to a \\emph{rotating $2$-adic target} --- with death iff the\nreading is odd; (3) under Haar measure the round process is\n\\emph{exactly} i.i.d.: survival probability $\\tfrac13$ per round,\ngeometric laws on every fiber (proved via the census lemma; the\nfreshness slope is $2\\cdot3^{\\#\\text{letters}}$), and surviving rounds\ndrift \\emph{upward} at $+0.6166$ bits per round in the mean --- the\napparent anti-correlations in finite enumerations are truncation\nartifacts; (4) Mersenne points $2^g-1$ survive their first round iff\n$g$ is odd and $\\vt(g-1)$ is even (pure LTE, deterministic); (5) the\n$\\{1,2\\}$ alphabet has an \\emph{entropy deficit}: confined-word growth\nis bounded by $2^{H(2-\\log_23)}=1.9712<2$ at \\emph{every} strip width,\nso the narrow-band dwell machinery applies to CIC-violators with no\nwidth cutoff --- the allowed region of the $(D,\\varepsilon)$ phase\ndiagram is empty for them; (6) empirically, the least integer\nsurviving $D$ letters grows like $2^{D/2.2}$. The remaining wall is a\nsingle scalar parity sequence read from provably fresh bits.\n\\end{abstract}\n\n\\section{Reduction to divergent $\\{1,2\\}$-orbits}\n\n\\begin{lemma}[Convergent orbits satisfy the CIC]\\label{lem:conv}\nIf the Syracuse orbit of $n_0>1$ reaches $1$, it takes a letter\n$b\\ge4$ at its last step before $1$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n$S(y)=1$ means $3y+1=2^b$, i.e.\\ $y=(4^k-1)/3$ with $b=2k$ (only even\n$b$ give integers). $k=1$ is $y=1$; every entry from $y\\ne1$ has\n$b=2k\\ge4$.\n\\end{proof}\n\n\\begin{corollary}\\label{cor:red}\nA CIC-violator is either a nontrivial positive cycle with all letters\nin $\\{1,2\\}$ --- excluded in all computationally verified ranges, and\nperiod-pinned by the Baker mechanism of the narrow-band note --- or a\n\\emph{divergent} orbit with all letters in $\\{1,2\\}$. The CIC is\nhenceforth the statement that no divergent $\\{1,2\\}$-orbit exists.\n\\end{corollary}\n\n\\section{The round chain and its LTE normal form}\n\n\\begin{theorem}[Round chain]\\label{thm:chain}\nLet $x\\equiv3\\pmod4$ be a $1$-run start, $g=\\vt(x+1)$, $\\ell=g-1$,\n$m=(x+1)/2^g$ odd. Set $v=\\vt(3^\\ell m-1)$. Then the next letters of\n$x$ are exactly $1^\\ell\\,2^{\\lfloor v/2\\rfloor}$ followed by: a letter\n$b\\ge3$ if $v$ is odd (\\emph{death}), or a new $1$-run if $v$ is even\n(\\emph{survival}), in which case, with $r=v/2$ and\n$u=(3^\\ell m-1)/2^v$,\n\\[\nm'=\\frac{3^ru+1}{2^{\\,\\vt(3^ru+1)}},\\qquad\n\\ell'=\\vt(3^ru+1),\n\\]\nare the parameters of the next round. Moreover the reading has the\nLTE normal form\n\\[\nv=\\vt(3^\\ell m-1)=\\vt\\bigl(m-3^{-\\ell}\\bigr):\n\\]\neach survival event is an alignment reading of the fresh multiplier\n$m$ against the rotating $2$-adic target $3^{-\\ell}\\in\\mathbb Z_2^\\times$.\n(Machine-verified: $5000$ rounds, letters, death criterion and\n$(g',m')$ all exact; LTE form on $2000$ random $(\\ell,m)$.)\n\\end{theorem}\n\n\\begin{proof}\nThe $-1$ clock gives the run $1^\\ell$ ending at $y$ with\n$y-1=2(3^\\ell m-1)$, so $h=\\vt(y-1)=1+v$; the $+1$ clock gives the\n$2$-run of length $\\lfloor(h-1)/2\\rfloor=\\lfloor v/2\\rfloor$ with\nparity handoff: $h$ odd ($v$ even) hands to a $1$-run, $h$ even ($v$\nodd) forces $b\\ge3$. The terminal point is $z$ with\n$z+1=2(3^ru+1)$, giving $(g',m')$. The normal form is\n$\\vt(3^\\ell)\\,{=}\\,0$ plus invertibility of $3$ in $\\mathbb Z_2$.\n\\end{proof}\n\n\\begin{remark}\nThe CIC is thus: \\emph{no odd integer can feed the chain even\nreadings forever}. The targets $3^{-\\ell}$ rotate through the index-$4$\nsubgroup $\\langle3\\rangle\\subset(\\mathbb Z/2^j)^\\times$, and at scale\n$j$ the target depends only on $\\ell\\bmod2^{j-2}$ --- the\nlifting-the-exponent structure.\n\\end{remark}\n\n\\section{Exact Haar laws: the survival coin is i.i.d.}\n\n\\begin{theorem}[Freshness; exact i.i.d.\\ laws]\\label{thm:iid}\nCondition on the full data of rounds $1,\\dots,i$ (all letters and all\nread bits). Then the round-$(i{+}1)$ reading is exactly geometric:\n$\\mathbb P[v=k]=2^{-k}$ $(k\\ge1)$, hence\n\\[\n\\mathbb P[\\text{survive round}]=\\sum_{k\\ge2\\ \\mathrm{even}}2^{-k}\n=\\tfrac13\n\\]\nindependently across rounds; given survival,\n$\\mathbb P[r=t]=3\\cdot4^{-t}$ ($\\mathbb E[r]=\\tfrac43$) and the next\ndepth is $\\mathbb P[g'=j]=2^{-(j-1)}$ ($\\mathbb E[\\ell']=2$).\n\\end{theorem}\n\n\\begin{proof}[Proof sketch]\nWrite the unread part of $m$ as $m=a+2^{w}s$ with $s$ the free (Haar)\nparameter. Through the round, every derived quantity is affine in $s$\nwith slope of the exact form $2\\cdot3^{B}\\cdot s$ ($B$ = letters\nconsumed): $u=u_0+2\\cdot3^{\\ell}s$, $3^ru+1=T_0+2\\cdot3^{\\ell+r}s$,\nand after extracting $2^{g'}$ and conditioning, $m'=m_0'+2\\cdot3^{B}s'$\n--- the same form, renormalized. The census lemma of the ghost-clock\nnote (slope valuation $\\gamma=1\\le\\beta$) then gives the exact\ngeometric law of each reading on each fiber, by induction over\nrounds. (This is the orbit-parameterization slope $2\\cdot3^{D}$ of\narXiv:2603.11066 composed with the census lemma; it generalizes that\nmanuscript's Carry Contamination Theorem from mod-$8$ equidistribution\nof one round to exact i.i.d.\\ laws of the whole process.)\n\\end{proof}\n\n\\noindent\\emph{Verification.} Exact enumeration of all $1$-run-start\nresidue classes modulo $2^{24}$, counting only classes whose round\noutcomes are class-determined: round-$1$ survival\n$1398024/4194144=0.333328$, round-$2$ $0.332689$. Deeper rounds show\n$0.322$, $0.272$, $0.125$ --- this is \\emph{truncation bias}, not\nanti-correlation: the determinedness filter caps the current reading\nat the remaining bit budget, and a geometric law truncated at an odd\ncutoff has even-mass below $\\tfrac13$ (e.g.\\ $2/7$ at cutoff $3$). Any\nempirical ``two-round anti-correlation'' at finite modulus has this\norigin; under Haar the coin is exactly fair-thirds and i.i.d.\n\n\\begin{corollary}[Survivors ascend]\\label{cor:ascend}\nConditioned on survival, the mean drift per round is\n\\[\n(\\log_23-1)\\,\\mathbb E[\\ell]-(2-\\log_23)\\,\\mathbb E[r]\n=2(0.58496)-\\tfrac43(0.41504)=+0.6166\\ \\text{bits},\n\\]\ni.e.\\ $+0.185$ bits per letter (verified: $+0.6164$ over the\nenumerated survivor classes). Haar-typical points die (density\n$(1/3)^j$ after $j$ rounds, so $\\mathcal C_\\infty$ is a measure-zero\nCantor set), while the surviving fibers drift upward at a definite\nrate: a positive CIC-violator, if one exists, lives in an exponentially\nthin set \\emph{and} is statistically forced toward divergence ---\nconsistent with \\cref{cor:red}.\n\\end{corollary}\n\n\\section{Deterministic sub-families: Mersenne LTE}\n\n\\begin{theorem}[Mersenne first round]\\label{thm:mersenne}\nFor $x=2^g-1$ ($m=1$, $\\ell=g-1$) the reading is fully deterministic:\n$v=\\vt(3^{g-1}-1)$ equals $1$ if $g$ is even, and $2+\\vt(g-1)$ if $g$\nis odd (LTE). Hence $2^g-1$ survives its first round iff $g$ is odd\nand $\\vt(g-1)$ is even. (Verified $g\\le60$: survivors\n$g\\in\\{5,13,17,21,29,37,45,49,53\\}$, i.e.\\\n$g-1\\equiv2^{2t}\\bmod2^{2t+1}$.)\n\\end{theorem}\n\n\\begin{remark}\nThe truncated ghosts are precisely the points whose readings are\n\\emph{not} fresh --- and there LTE decides everything. Freshness\n(\\cref{thm:iid}) and LTE determinism (\\cref{thm:mersenne}) are the two\npoles of the problem: the wall is exactly the regime between them.\n\\end{remark}\n\n\\section{The entropy deficit of the $\\{1,2\\}$ alphabet}\n\n\\begin{theorem}[Entropy deficit]\\label{thm:deficit}\nLet $N^{12}_D(p)$ count $D$-confined valuation words of length $p$\nover the alphabet $\\{1,2\\}$, and\n$\\lambda_{12}(D)=\\lim N^{12}_D(p)^{1/p}$. Then for \\emph{every} $D$,\n\\[\n\\theta_{12}(D)=\\log_2\\lambda_{12}(D)\\ \\le\\ H(2-\\log_23)=0.97907<1 ,\n\\]\nsince confinement pins the letter-$1$ frequency at $2-\\log_23$ and\nbinary words at fixed frequency number at most\n$2^{H(q)p+o(p)}$. Exact quantized counts (rotation-driven recursion,\n$p=2000$): $\\theta_{12}=0.521,\\ 0.753,\\ 0.889,\\ 0.955,\\ 0.973$ at\n$D=0.8,\\ 1.2,\\ 2,\\ 4,\\ 8$, increasing toward the ceiling.\n\\end{theorem}\n\n\\begin{corollary}[All-width dwell for CIC-violators]\\label{cor:dwell}\nAn acyclic $\\{1,2\\}$-orbit dwells at most\n$C\\,(WY)^{0.980}$ consecutive steps in \\emph{any} band $[Y,WY]$ ---\nincluding arbitrarily wide bands. (Proof: repetition rigidity plus the\npigeonhole of the narrow-band theorem, with $N^{12}$ in place of $N$;\nno $D^*$ cutoff because $\\theta_{12}<1$ uniformly.) In particular, a\nsingle excursion of a divergent $\\{1,2\\}$-orbit below height $X$ lasts\nat most $C\\,X^{0.980}$ steps, and the allowed (red) region of the\n$(D,\\varepsilon)$ phase diagram is \\emph{empty} for CIC-violators: the\nfull-alphabet escape hatch at $D>D^*=1.246$ is closed by the missing\nletters.\n\\end{corollary}\n\n\\section{Survival champions}\n\nThe least $n_0\\equiv3\\pmod4$ surviving $D$ letters (seeds to\n$2^{26}$):\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c|ccccccc}\n\\toprule\nD & 4\\text{--}19 & 20 & 28 & 36 & 39\\text{--}44\\\\\n\\midrule\n\\min n_0 & 27 & 4591 & 31911 & 517191 & 687871\\\\\nD/\\log_2 n_0 & \\le4.0 & 1.64 & 1.87 & 1.90 & 2.0\\text{--}2.3\\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{array}\n\\]\nThe ratio $D/\\log_2(\\min n_0)$ stabilizes near $2$: empirically the\nleast survivor of depth $D$ has height about $2^{D/2.2}$. We record:\n\n\\begin{conjecture}[Champion growth]\\label{conj:champ}\nThere is $c>0$ with $\\min\\{n_0:\\text{$n_0$ survives $D$ letters}\\}\\ge\n2^{cD}$. Granting this, every CIC-violating orbit satisfies\n$x_n\\ge2^{c'n}$: violators must flee to infinity at a definite\nexponential rate, closing the CIC for all sub-exponential orbits.\n\\end{conjecture}\n\n\\section{Where the wall now stands}\n\nThe CIC has been compressed to: \\emph{a single scalar parity sequence\n--- the readings $\\vt(m_i-3^{-\\ell_i})$ --- cannot be even forever\nalong any positive orbit}. The readings are provably i.i.d.\\\nfair-thirds coins on Haar fibers (\\cref{thm:iid}); they are provably\ndeterministic, and lethal in explicit congruence patterns, on the\nghost-aligned sub-families (\\cref{thm:mersenne}); the counting\nmachinery confines any violator to perpetual fast ascent with empty\nphase-diagram refuge (\\cref{thm:deficit}, \\cref{cor:ascend}); and the\nchampion data suggest violators must be exponentially large in their\nsurvival depth. What is missing is precisely the\ndistributional-to-pointwise step --- the same quenched calibration\nwall, now localized to one coin.\n\n\\begin{thebibliography}{9}\n\\bibitem{chang} E.~Y.~Chang, \\emph{Exploring Collatz Dynamics with\nHuman-LLM Collaboration}, arXiv:2603.11066v6 (2026).\n\\bibitem{gc} J.~A.~Janik, \\emph{The Universal Ghost Clock}, companion\nnote (2026).\n\\bibitem{tc} J.~A.~Janik, \\emph{Two Clocks: the $\\pm1$ meters, depth\nsupply, and unconditional escape bounds}, companion note (2026).\n\\bibitem{nb} J.~A.~Janik, \\emph{Narrow-band exclusion and the\n$(D,\\varepsilon)$ phase diagram}, companion note (2026).\n\\end{thebibliography}\n\n\\end{document}\n